submittedParameters.prompt:
Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: production game art, isometric industry compound and detachable mechanical moving parts. Exactly NINE separate objects arranged evenly in 3 rows and3 columns, whole square target2048, genuine transparent alpha.
Keep each object entirely inside middle75% of its cell, wide clean transparent gutters, no parts touching. No background, no text, numbers, grids, UI panels or icons. Camera orthographic isometric2:1 from southeast, bright soft daylight from upper-left. Match attached Taoist chibi style: fine jade-green/teal, warm ivory, gold/copper/wood, rounded hand-painted details, no glossy CGI. Third reference for world material fidelity.
Cell1 top-left: COMPLETE sugar mine industry compound, exposed mound of pale ivory sugar crystals, copper/wood sugar sifting conveyor, small jade-roof machinery house and cream sugar sacks on thin stone rhombus yard.
Remaining8 cells are DETACHABLE MOVING PARTS ONLY, no ground or support buildings: draw parts large and completely unobstructed so animation can pivot/translate them later:
cell2 top-middle: single sturdy round wooden mine-winding wheel with8 spokes, bronze hub and metal rim, wheel face viewed slightly isometric so round face appears gentle ellipse; no tower or cable.
cell3 top-right: single horizontal long jade/copper horsehead oil pumpjack rocking beam, rounded heavy curved head at LEFT, circular brass pivot hub near RIGHT; no vertical support, ground, cables or base.
cell4 middle-left: copper and ivory electrical coil switch assembly with two brass electrode terminals and a small jade base, no spark emission, no building;
cell5 middle-middle: single heavy rectangular warm-gold toy-factory press platen with jade inset and two short guide sleeves, no factory or base;
cell6 middle-right: a single connected curved stream of translucent pale-mint liquid plastic flowing from upper-left to a small pooled splash lower-right; no nozzle or reservoir hardware, delicate ivory highlights, coherent connected stream, no detached droplets;
cell7 bottom-left: a single round copper bubble-making ring nozzle with jade collar seen in isometric from above, empty transparent center, no actual bubbles, no supporting machine;
cell8 bottom-middle: a single thick vertical caramel/copper helical quarry auger with jade gearbox on its upper end, lower spiral tip pointing down, no ground or crane;
cell9 bottom-right: a single rectangular shallow sugar-sieve tray, warm ivory mesh with brass border and two short side handles, holding a small layer of pale sugar grains, no supports or ground.
All9 objects complete and distinct. Keep thin delicate clean alpha edges; not sticker outlines.

